+Codex Plus Ultracode is a root-session workflow setting, independent of reasoning effort. At the start of every root turn and after compaction, read `codex-plus ultracode status --thread $CODEX_THREAD_ID --json`. Use only the effective snapshot bound to this exact admitted turn and daemon generation; requested or pending state does not activate the mode. When effective on, follow the complete policy returned by status. When off or unavailable, follow ordinary user and repository instructions. Native children follow their parent's bounded brief instead of calling this command. Mode changes apply to future unadmitted turns; steering keeps the current turn's snapshot. Existing goal checkpoints, report-only recovery and newer user direction retain priority. Ultracode never expands permission to publish, merge, install or change shared configuration.
